# What `vite build --mode desktop-test` reads: a desktop build that talks to
# the server on your own machine instead of the deployed one.
#
# This exists because the shipped desktop app cannot be pointed anywhere else.
# VITE_API_URL is baked into the bundle at build time and CIPHER_DESKTOP_URL is
# read by `option_env!`, so a installed Cipher is production, permanently. A
# test build is the only way to drive the desktop shell against local accounts.
#
# Built with tauri.test.conf.json, which gives it its own name and identifier
# so it installs beside the real Cipher rather than over it, widens the CSP to
# allow this host, and points the updater at nothing so a test build can never
# offer itself as an upgrade to the real one.
#
# Run the API first: `npm run dev:server` at the repo root.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3000
VITE_AUTH_MODE=bearer
VITE_BACKEND=http
VITE_PLATFORM=desktop
